{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The New Waiter", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Getting Comfortable", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "  Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inseparable phrasal verbs are very common. The verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span></li> <li>take off = leave the ground  <br/>         The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to hang around\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to spend time with someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look down on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to feel superior to someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look up to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to admire someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk back\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to answer impolitely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to put up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to tolerate\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I really looked up to my mentor. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For example, he gave me pointers on how to put up with difficult customers in any situation.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Should and Be Supposed To ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal  <span class=\"strong\">should</span> or the  structure  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the present or future that are expected to happen. <br/><br/> The structure is:<br/><br/>  Subject + To be + supposed to + verb<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Sharing information with their new colleagues is something they're <span class=\"strong\">supposed to do</span> .</span> <br/><br/>  **Pronunciation tip**:<br/> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br/><br/> Like this:<br/> Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You're supposed to keep smiling even when you have to deal with terrible patrons. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Obviously, you shouldn't talk back either.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "trainee", "type": "name"}, {"content": " someone undergoing training", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a new trainee, you should spend some time with a senior waiter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about customer service.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to hang around", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time with someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a new trainee, you should hang around with a senior waiter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to look down on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel superior to someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope the senior waiters won't look down on me because I'm a trainee.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to look up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "respect, admire someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had a mentor in Colombia that I really looked up to you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to talk back", "type": "name"}, {"content": "respond in an impolite way to an adult", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Servers should not talk back to customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to put up with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tolerate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to put up with difficult customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "impeccable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without any faults", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  His service is impeccable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "unobtrusive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unnoticeable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is an unobtrusive server. Patrons barely notice him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a paragraph 6 to 8 sentences long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Who was your most important mentor when you were young?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Why did you pick this person?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What problems did your mentor help you with?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use at least five phrasal verbs. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your stories with your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rules and regulations. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about life experiences. ", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about rules and regulations. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about life experiences. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that I'm supposed to do and things that are  supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What are some rules and regu